    "id": "r1",
    "name": "Garage Buona Forchetta",
    "address": "3001 Beech St, San Diego, CA 92102",
    "cuisine": "Italian",
    "rating": 4.7,
    "tags": [
      "restaurant",
      "bar"
    ],
    "lat": 32.68531518270564,
    "lng": -117.17890793621442,
    "description": "<p>Buona Forchetta is a pillar of the community in every San Diego neighborhood that it is in, but this location will always have a pizza my heart. Whether you are here for their authentic Neapolitan pizza's, home-made pasta, or any of the Italian classics that they offer, you cannot go wrong.&nbsp;</p><h3>My Order</h3><ul><li>MARGHERITA — the benchmark pizza</li><li>SOTTOTERRA — a savory and tangy salad featuring a fresh organic greens base topped with a pre-mixed blend of sautéed carrots, fennel, parsnips, and onions, all finished with creamy goat cheese and a zesty homemade Dijon mustard vinaigrette.</li><li>TIRAMISU — absolute perfection.&nbsp;</li><li>And literally any of the pasta/sauce/toppings</li></ul><p>And after you've carb loaded and are starting to feel the post-comida coma, Downtown Coronado is a lovely — and romantic ;) — spot for a long walk with the beach not too far away.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
