  {
    "id": "r9",
    "name": "Pomegranate",
    "address": "4210 30th St, San Diego, CA 92104",
    "cuisine": "Russian",
    "rating": 4.3,
    "lat": 32.7554976219723,
    "lng": -117.13963819826232,
    "tags": [
      "restaurant"
    ],
    "description": "<p>One of the few Russian kitchens in San Diego worth making a habit of. The borscht is the deep, almost black kind — beet-forward, finished with a spoonful of smetana and a good amount of dill. The pelmeni are made in-house and arrive in broth that has been going for a while.</p><h3>The order</h3><ul><li>Borscht — the version that takes two days to make</li><li>Pelmeni, beef and pork, in broth</li><li>Blini with smoked salmon and smetana</li></ul><p>Order the house compote. Don't argue about it.</p>",
    "createdAt": "2026-03-15"
  },
