  {
    "id": "r30",
    "name": "The Grass Skirt",
    "address": "910 Grand Ave, San Diego, CA 92109",
    "cuisine": "Tiki Bar",
    "rating": 4.7,
    "lat": 32.79862,
    "lng": -117.25117,
    "tags": [
      "bar"
    ],
    "description": "<p>Pacific Beach tiki bar hidden behind Good Time Poke — the burger joint at the front is the door. Through it: bamboo, thatch, tropical lighting, and one of the better rum programs in San Diego. The drinks are serious inside the tiki tradition: house-made orgeat, fresh citrus, layered rum builds. The Zombie is not a novelty here.</p><h3>The order</h3><ul><li>Zombie — the classic, executed correctly, and the two-drink limit is the policy and the correct one</li><li>Mai Tai — the benchmark for any tiki bar, and this version earns it</li><li>Whatever the seasonal special is — usually built around a house infusion</li></ul><p>Book ahead for weekend nights. The room is intimate, the line is real, and the walk-in wait can push past an hour.</p>",
    "createdAt": "2026-06-01"
  },
